Alfred Firefox Assistant
========================

This product is a modified version of "Firefox Assistant for Alfred"
(alfred-firefox), originally created by Dean Jackson.

  Original work:  https://github.com/deanishe/alfred-firefox
  Original author: Dean Jackson <deanishe@deanishe.net>
  Licence:        MIT (see LICENCE.txt)

Modifications
-------------

Copyright (c) 2024-2026 Andres Mena Godino

The following changes were made to the original work. Files derived from the
original carry both the original copyright notice and a "Modifications
Copyright" line.

  * Rewrote the matching engine: searches tab titles *and* URLs, splits the
    query into terms that may match in any order (logical AND), matches each
    term against individual tokens, splits CamelCase, and adds a scoring bonus
    for title matches.
  * Unified the `tab` keyword so that matching history and recently-closed
    tabs are folded into the open-tab results and de-duplicated by URL.
  * Added most-recently-used ordering and recency tie-breaking throughout, and
    suppressed Alfred result UIDs so the workflow's own ordering is preserved.
  * Added relative "last opened" timestamps to tab, history and closed-tab
    results.
  * Added Firefox tab-group support (Firefox 139+): group name and colour on
    tab results, plus a new `tg` keyword that browses and searches tab groups
    and switches to one. New files: tabgroups.go, tabgroups_test.go.
  * Added extension commands "all-tab-groups" and "activate-tab-group", with a
    fallback that reconstructs the group list from per-tab fields so the
    feature degrades gracefully against older builds of the extension.
  * Added tab and URL actions: Close Tab, Close Duplicate Tabs, Mute/Unmute
    Tab, Move Tab to New Window, Copy Link as Markdown, Copy Title.
  * Added relevance ranking for bookmark, history and download results, and
    removed the three-character minimum from the history and bookmarklet
    keywords.
  * Fixed the native-messaging server so it exits cleanly when the browser
    quits instead of leaving an orphaned process, and so it removes a stale
    socket on startup.
  * Disabled the auto-updater and removed the "install the public add-on"
    menu entry, so this build is never silently replaced by the original.
  * Added unit tests for the matching engine and the tab-group feature.

